---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Field Notes — GeoSmart" description="Field notes, geological explanations and learning notes from Camila Fernández's journey through geology and Norway.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-kicker">Geology · Norway · Learning</div>
      <h1>Field Notes</h1>
      <p class="muted">Short geological explanations, field observations and notes from the journey — written to be useful whether you already speak geology or are just curious.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container field-notes-layout">
      <article class="note-feature note-article-card">
        <div class="note-meta"><span class="card-tag">Geophysics</span><span>·</span><span>Coming soon</span></div>
        <h2>Why does seismic interpretation actually matter?</h2>
        <p class="lead">Seismic data is more than pretty lines on a screen. It is a window into the Earth's history and a way of building hypotheses about structures we cannot see directly.</p>
        <div class="article-teaser"><span>WHAT I’LL COVER</span><p>Reflections · horizons · faults · geological reasoning · uncertainty</p></div>
        <div class="note-footer"><span>Field Note 01</span><span>Read soon →</span></div>
      </article>

      <div class="note-list note-grid">
        <article class="note note-card">
          <div class="note-meta"><span class="card-tag">Norway</span><span>Field · Trondheim</span></div>
          <h3>Geology in Trondheim</h3>
          <p>What stands out when a geology student starts paying attention to the rocks, landscapes and geological history around Trondheim.</p>
          <div class="note-footer"><span>Field Note 02</span><span>Coming soon</span></div>
        </article>
        <article class="note note-card">
          <div class="note-meta"><span class="card-tag">Sedimentology</span><span>Learning</span></div>
          <h3>Reading a sedimentary log</h3>
          <p>A beginner-friendly look at how observations become a sedimentary interpretation — and where the uncertainty starts.</p>
          <div class="note-footer"><span>Field Note 03</span><span>Coming soon</span></div>
        </article>
        <article class="note note-card">
          <div class="note-meta"><span class="card-tag">Energy</span><span>Subsurface</span></div>
          <h3>What makes a good reservoir?</h3>
          <p>Porosity, permeability and the geological story behind reservoir quality, explained without drowning in jargon.</p>
          <div class="note-footer"><span>Field Note 04</span><span>Coming soon</span></div>
        </article>
        <article class="note note-card">
          <div class="note-meta"><span class="card-tag">Learning</span><span>Student life</span></div>
          <h3>Things I wish I knew before studying geology</h3>
          <p>A collection of lessons from the first years: fieldwork, maps, mistakes, software and learning how to think like a geologist.</p>
          <div class="note-footer"><span>Field Note 05</span><span>Coming soon</span></div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
